ank\"\n                                   href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_course_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\"\n                                   class=\"btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm\">\n                                    Learn More\n                                <\/a>\n                            <\/div>\n                        <\/div>\n                    <\/div>\n\n                \n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n    <\/section>\n\n    \n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Types of SEO<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Let\u2019s understand the different types of SEO in digital marketing, in detail:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. On-page SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On-page SEO<\/a> means optimizing each web page and element on a website, such as content, images, HTML code, etc., to boost its search engine rankings on SERPs and drive quality traffic. It involves making every element more relevant and appealing to users and search engines.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of On-page SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Some common on-page SEO elements are as follows:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Keyword Research: <\/strong>Keyword research is the process of finding and researching relevant search phrases used by people to search for a query or product online. Marketers strategically use these keywords in content to improve the rankings of web pages and increase brand awareness.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Title Tag: <\/strong>It refers to the clickable headline that we see in search results. An optimized title tag must include relevant keywords and should be concise yet descriptive.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Meta Description: <\/strong>Meta description is the brief summary of a web page that we see below the title tag in search results. It should be compelling and informative to make users click on the link.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Header Tags:<\/strong> They provide a property structure to the content on a website or blog and showcase the importance of each section. Used as H1, H2, H3, and so on, they highlight important keywords and phrases.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>URL Structure: <\/strong>Uniform Resource Locator (URL) is a web address, allowing users to access each page. It includes relevant keywords and follows a logical structure so that search engines can determine the content of the web page and crawl it for the ranking.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Content: <\/strong>Content creation is a key component of different types of SEO, including off-page, on-page, voice search, image SEO, social media SEO, etc. Marketers should optimize website or blog content to boost its ranking. Content optimization includes adding relevant keywords, writing quality and engaging content, and making it readable for the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/target-audience\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">target audience<\/a>.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Images:<\/strong> Websites use images to improve user experience and make web pages visually appealing. However, images should be compressed and have descriptive alt tags to be SEO-friendly.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Internal Links: <\/strong>These links connect different web pages of the same website, enabling search engines to understand the correct structure of the website and distribute link equity.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>External Links: <\/strong>They connect a web page of your website to other websites. External links are used to publish guest blogs, provide additional information, add cite sources, or build relationships with other brands and websites.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Page Formatting: <\/strong>Writing quality content and creating attractive images are crucial to optimize a website. However, it is also crucial to spruce up the content. Google assesses web pages on its appearance and look, checking it\u2019s full of ads and popups to rank them on its <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/serp\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SERPs<\/a>.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Off-page SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/off-page-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Off-page SEO<\/a> focuses on promoting a website on other platforms and sites. It includes social media marketing, link building, email marketing, etc. unlike on-page SEO that is more about a website\u2019s structure and content, off-page SEO involves techniques to boost website\u2019s ranking on search engines by optimizing factors outside the website itself. The aim of this type of SEO is to increase a website\u2019s reputation, authority, and relevance, which is important to drive organic traffic.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Off-page SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Here are a few vital off-page SEO elements marketers focus on:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-are-backlinks\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Backlinks<\/a>:<\/strong> These are links you get from other websites to your specific web page. Backlinks allow search engines to assess the authority and popularity of a website.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>H.A.R.O: <\/strong>Help a Reporter Out (H.A.R.O.) is an online service that connects reporters and media professionals so they can collect quotes to curate blogs, articles, press releases, and other types of content. In simple terms, it refers to addressing reporters\u2019 queries to gain backlinks and media attention.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Social Media: <\/strong>Increased social media engagement, such as comments, likes, shares, and feedback, can boost the visibility and popularity of a website. It is also an effective way to build stronger and long-term relationships with potential customers while driving quality traffic to the website.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Brand Mentions: <\/strong>When the name of the brand or product is mentioned on other websites, forums, social media,and other channels, it adds to brand awareness and enances the reputation of the website.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Competitor Analysis: <\/strong>Marketers constantly keep a close watch on activities of their competitors, analyzing their digital marketing and SEO techniques to optimize their own. This helps them understand keywords competitors are using, content they are publishing, and campaigns they are building.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Guest Blogs:<\/strong> Marketers often write and publish articles on other websites that link back to their own websites; these are known as guest postings. They build links, increase brand awareness, and drive traffic.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read:<\/strong> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-benefits\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Top 8 Benefits of SEO Marketing (Importance)<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Technical SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/technical-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical SEO<\/a> includes different types of SEO techniques to improve the technical aspects of a website so that search engines can easily crawl and index it for improved search engine rankings. It includes improving page loading speed, setting up redirects, configuring robot.txt file, making the website mobile-friendly, and so on. Technical SEO makes a site more accessible to search engines and users.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Technical SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>The following are the key elements of technical SEO:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Website Structure: <\/strong>The website should follow a proper and clear structure so people can easily navigate it. There must be a logical hierarchy of different web pages and categories, allowing search engines to crawl and index it without much hassle.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Website Speed: <\/strong>The website&#8217;s loading speed, including its text, images, and videos, determines its ranking in SERPs. If a website takes too long to load, it can lead to a higher bounce rate and lower search engine rankings.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Identification of Crawl Errors: <\/strong>To improve your site\u2019s rankings and overall visibility, you need to identify crawl errors that hamper performance. This is a great way to find and resolve errors, such as broken links, missing pages, etc., making the website and its content easily accessible to search engines.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Mobile-friendliness: <\/strong>People now rely on their smartphones to access apps or websites. Therefore, your website should be mobile-friendly so that more users can access it on their mobile devices.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Security: <\/strong>Your website should be secure to keep user data safe and prevent hacking. You can protect your website from cyber-attacks by using a secure hosting provider, updating software, and implementing SSL encryption.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Audit of Duplicate Content: <\/strong>Two write-ups that are exactly the same or identical can also affect your search engine ranking and credibility. So, audit your content regularly to find the same content on the internet and optimize it for improved search engine rankings.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>XML Sitemap: <\/strong>It is a file that lists important web pages, so that search engines can discover and index them easily.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Keyword Cannibalization Audit: <\/strong>It refers to identifying multiple pages on the website competing for the same keyword and fixing this issue. Such instances can dilute the online visibility of the website and affect its organic performance.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Local SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/local-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Local SEO<\/a> comprises strategies to optimize a website for local search results. If you have a brick-and-mortar store and want to attract clients to visit it, you need to work on local SEO to improve its visibility and popularity. It targets audiences based on location by promoting a business across directories, local search engines, and maps.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It helps you get more clients and traffic to yoru store or office. Local SEO techniques include building citation and backlinks from local sources, optimzing Google My Business profile, adding local keywords, managing online reviews, and ensuring local business listings. Basically, these types of SEO optimization techniques aim to attract the local customers to your nearby store.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Local SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Here are a few local SEO elements you need to pay attention to:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Google My Business (GMB) Account:<\/strong> You need to create and enhance your Google My Business listing to improve the online visibility of your business in local search results and on&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google Maps. Add all the necessary details, such as the name and address of the business, contact details, operating hours, and pictures.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Local Citations: <\/strong>Register your business with trusted directories and platforms, such as Yelp, Foursquare, etc. Your listings should be accurate and consistent across all platforms and channels so that search engines can confirm your address and credibility.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>On-page SEO: <\/strong>Develop and publish content for local search results and make it relevant to your business location. The name, address, and phone number of your business must be consistent and displayed correctly.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Online Reviews: <\/strong>Encourage your existing clients to share their feedback on different sites, such as Google, Yelp, and more, to enhance your marketing efforts.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Backlinks: <\/strong>Get quality links to your website from high-authority and reputable regional websites and trade publications.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/content-marketing\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Content Marketing<\/a>:<\/strong> Curate informative, optimized, and top-notch content that targets the local audience and showcases your subject-matter competence.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Mobile Optimization:<\/strong> Optimize your website for all operating systems and mobile devices as users now prefer their phones to look for queries, products, or services.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Social Media: <\/strong>Create social media profiles to connect with native users and promote your products and services.<\/p>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cracking-meta-google-ads-2026-data-automation-attribution?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-07-31T112145_393_1785491880854_775860.webp\" alt=\"Cracking Meta &amp; Google Ads 2026 - Data, Automation &amp; Attribution\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item