  <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cybersecurity-professional-career-roadmap-2026-2?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-08-05T122121_005_1786351858212_930412.webp\" alt=\"Cybersecurity Professional Career Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <\/div>\n        <\/div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. E-commerce SEO&nbsp;<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>E-commerce stores also need to achieve top ranks on SERPs to attract more potential and quality customers. Whenever a user searches for a product, the search engine shows the most relevant online stores offering the same product. Hence comes c-commerce SEO, which is among the top 4 types of SEO and is used to optimize online stores. It enhances the visibility and search engine rankings of e-commerce websites by focusing on different elements, such as category pages, blogs, product pages, etc. Similar to any other SEO tactic, it also intends to drive more organic traffic to the website and boost sales. It also includes improving website architecture, competitors\u2019 research and analysis, and homepage SEO.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of E-commerce SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>To optimize online stores and improve their visibility across search engines, e-commerce SEO focuses on the following elements:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Keyword Research: <\/strong>Marketers identify and target relevant keywords related to different products offered by their e-commerce store.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>On-page SEO: <\/strong>It includes optimizing the website for search engines, including its product and category pages, meta tags, image alt text, and headers.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>User-friendly URLs: <\/strong>The URL of each web page should be user-friendly and clear, including relevant keywords and describing the content accurately.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Site Structure: <\/strong>The site structure must be intuitive and logical so users can navigate it easily.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Product Descriptions: <\/strong>Each product should have a compelling and informative description that also includes relevant keywords.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Mobile Optimization: <\/strong>The e-commerce website must be optimized for mobile devices to reach more users.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>6. Mobile SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>As the name suggests, <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/mobile-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">mobile SEO<\/a> refers to the process of optimizing a website for mobile devices and tablets. It is not exactly a different type of SEO strategy but a subset of SEO that is specific to mobile phones.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>More than 60% of searches happen on smartphones. Hence, Google has created a mobile-first index to assess how mobile-friendly a website is. A bad user experience on mobile devices means users will never return to that page. Therefore, it\u2019s necessary that you offer the best and seamless experience to users, which is possible through mobile SEO. It aims to improve the structure, style, and loading speed of web pages when people use smartphones to access a site.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>A few essential elements to consider for mobile SEO are:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Web page loading speed.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Format of the content for viewing on smartphones.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mobile compatibility<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ease of use<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>User experience<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>No aggressive advertising or popups that can hamper the overall experience.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>7. International SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>International SEO is used to optimize multilingual websites or content to enhance their online visibility and ranking in global search results for users in different countries. Websites offering content in different languages use specific SEO techniques to enable search engines to index their content better. These are known as international SEO techniques. Their goal is to make such websites more accessible to the global audience and increase engagement, conversions, and traffic.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This is one of the main types of SEO used by big companies and global brands to drive more organic traffic from different regions and countries. To launch successful international SEO campaigns, you need to meet the requirements of the target audience and cater to the global market\u2019s cultural context so they can make transactions in their currency and interact with your brand in their language.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Moreover, make sure to use the right format for the date and time according to the region. You also need to communicate in the native language of the users while addressing their queries to offer the best experience.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of International SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>As mentioned, international SEO is a technique for optimizing a website for better performance in search engines across multiple languages and countries. It includes various tactics and methods that make a website relevant, appealing, and accessible in different locations.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>International SEO is the process of optimizing a website to ensure that it performs well in search engine results across multiple countries and languages. It involves strategies and techniques to make a website accessible, relevant, and appealing to users in different geographic locations. The key elements of international SEO are:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Localized Content: <\/strong>It involves creating linguistically and culturally appropriate content for prospects, including adapting images, focusing on local customs, and translating content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Hreflang Tags: <\/strong>It includes implementing the hreflang tag to tell search engines which region and language you are targeting with each page. These tags are used to avoid duplicate content on the website.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Country Code Top-Level Domains (ccTLDs): <\/strong>You need to use country-specific domain extensions, such as .de and .uk, to optimize different website variations and showcase their relevance to a specific geographical location.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Currency and Pricing: <\/strong>Marketers ensure that product prices are displayed in the local currency. They also adapt to different pricing strategies to show price variations based on regions and market conditions.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Geotargeting: <\/strong>This element focuses on using geotargeting settings like Google Search Console to change the country you are targeting for a specific version of your website.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Subdirectories and Subdomains: <\/strong>You need to organize your international content through subdirectories and subdomains that separate each content by their area or language.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>8. Image SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Image SEO deals with optimizing images and image hosting platforms to enhance their search engine rankings and drive organic traffic. Although alt text is the most popular image SEO factor, there are more techniques that marketers use to make images SEO-friendly.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Image SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Image SEO focuses on optimizing images on a website to make them more responsive and increase their online visibility. This is one of the top SEO types used to attract and engage more users, leading to more traffic to the website and its enhanced performance. The key elements of image SEO are:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Image Sitemap: <\/strong>Marketers add images to he XML sitemap of the website to enable search engines to index images and associate them with the content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Compress and Resize Images: <\/strong>Large image files can hamper the performance of a website, making it slow and affecting user experience. Therefore, you need to optimize the size of images while maintaining their quality. For this, you can use compression techniques that reduce the size of image files without compromising on the quality.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>File Names: <\/strong>Add relevant and descriptive file name for each umage. Make sure that names are not generic. Go for specific and descriptive names that include keywords relevant to the content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Image Format: <\/strong>Your content should have appropriate images in suitable formats. For example, JPEG is used for photographs, PNG is best for images with transparency, and WebP, a modern format, compresses images and maintains top-notch quality.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Responsive Images: <\/strong>Responsiveness is a major factor considered by search engines while determining the mobile-friendliness of a website and evaluating it for rankings. Hence, images must be responsive to different screen sizes and devices.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Image Alt Text: <\/strong>Alt text is a brief description added to each image so search engines can crawl it and assess its relationship with the content. Also, it affects accessibiity of the website. So, add concise and clear alt text to all images.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-3af46680a8b3116c9c7fc1a2e5222802\"><strong>Explore These Essential SEO Topics<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-tools-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Keyword Research Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/technical-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Technical SEO Checklist<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/link-building-mistakes\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Link Building Mistakes<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-factors\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Factors<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/ai-seo-tools\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI SEO Tools<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/on-page-seo-checklist\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">On Page SEO Checklist<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>9. Voice SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>As virtual assistants and voice-activated devices, such as Alexa, Siri, etc., are gaining popularity, voice search is becoming more common. Hence, it is crucial for businesses and brands to make their websites compatible for voice search. Voice SEO optimizes websites and content for voice search. It improves a site\u2019s online visibility and accessibility by making it accessible to voice-activated devices. Voice search optimization is used for digital content to boost its search engine ranking.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Voice SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>The key elements of voice SEO are as follows:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conversational Content: <\/strong>Content must be written in the tone that people use in day-to-day conversations. It should provide direct answers to frequently asked queries.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Natural Language Keywords: <\/strong>Add natural language keywords to the content that people use while speaking, as search engines prefer sites that have more conversational content.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Local Optimization: <\/strong>Content should be optimized for local searches because most voice searches are location-specific. Add the name and address of your business and contact details on the website and update the details regularly.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>User Intent: <\/strong>Try to understand the user intent behind voice searches to optimize the website and content for navigational, informational, and transactional queries.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Featured Snippets: <\/strong>Optimize the website for featured snippets because many voice search responses are gathered from such information-rich snippets.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/seo-skills\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">20+ Key SEO Skills You Need to Succeed<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>10. Video SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>As we answer how many types of SEO are there, we can\u2019t ignore video SEO. It is used to optimize video content so it appears on the top of video streaming or video hosting platforms, such as YouTube and Instagram, in search results. Similar to any other SEO strategy, it also aims at boosting videos\u2019 rankings, drive traffic, and increase views.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Elements of Video SEO<\/strong><\/h4>\n\n\n\n<p>Vide SEO improves the visibility and rankings of video content. To achieve this, marketers have to focus on a few crucial elements, which are as follows:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Transcriptions and Closed Captions: <\/strong>Videos must have accurate captions and transcriptions to be accessible by more people and enable search engines to understand the content and purpose of videos.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Keyword Research: <\/strong>You use different tools to identify and choose the most relevant keywords for your videos. The selected keywords must suit your topic and have good search volumes.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Video Description: <\/strong>Videos must have detailed descriptions, providing context about the content of the video. Your description should have relevant keywords and links of reliable resources if needed.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Tags: <\/strong>There must be relevant and descriptive tags for videos to enable search engines to understand their context and discover them easily.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Video Title: <\/strong>Create interesting and keyword-rich titles for videos that represent their content and attract viewers.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Thumbnail Optimization: <\/strong>An eye-catching thumbnail is important for the video to entice users to click on it.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>11. Negative SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Negative SEO may not be the most ethical SEO practice, but brands and marketers use it in certain situations to achieve top rankings. The goal of negative SEO is to hamper competitors\u2019 search engine rankings to replace that position or gain benefits from their loss.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>There are several negative SEO techniques used by businesses, such as posting negative reviews and feedback on different platforms, hacking others\u2019 websites and building multiple low-quality links, etc. If a person involved in such malicious activities is identified, it can lead to legal ordeals. So, it\u2019s always recommended to stay away from negative SEO.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read: <\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/keyword-research-seo\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">How to Do Keyword Research for SEO? Strategy<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>12. White-hat SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>White-hat SEO includes all major types of SEO in digital marketing that abide by the guidelines and regulations of all major search engines, including Google, Bing, and Yahoo. These methods take time to yield results, so you need to be patient. However, once white-hat SEO starts working, you get sustainable and long-term results that build credibility and goodwill around your brand.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>White-hat SEO techniques comprise ethical practices to improve search engine rankings while regulating the integrity of the brand and website. The best part of this SEO type is there is no risk of getting the website banned by search engines if there are algorithm updates. So, we can say that white-hat SEO is low-risk and highly rewarding if done right.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>A few common examples of white-hat SEO are developing relevant and quality content, using keyword-rich meta tags, doing extensive keyword research, building links from high-authority links, offering top-notch content and services, developing an easy-to-navigate website, etc.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-d72f351059e80039135382f58233f821\"><strong>Explore Our Most Popular Marketing Courses<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/digital-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Digital Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/performance-marketing-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogTable&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Performance Marketing Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><tr><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SEO Course<\/a><\/td><td class=\"has-text-align-center\" data-align=\"center\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/ai-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=BlogInterlink&amp;utm_campaign=seo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">AI Course<\/a><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>13. Black-hat SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Black-hat SEO is the opposite of white-hat SEO, comprising techniques that exploit weaknesses in Google\u2019s search algorithm to get a higher rank on SERPs. These methods don\u2019t follow the regulations of search engines and resort to bad practices to get the website ahead, such as keyword stuffing, spammy or paid link building, cloaking to misguide crawlers, etc.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Such black-hat SEO methods may give instant results but can get your website blacklisted or affect its search engine ranking if detected by Google. Also, you achieve short-lived results even after taking such high risks. Therefore, it\u2019s best to avoid back-hat SEO.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>14. Gray-hat SEO<\/strong><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Gray-hat SEO includes tactics that are neither black-hat nor white-hat, so the terms and conditions regarding these practices are unclear. Marketers use gray-hat SEO to get quick results.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Google and other search engines don\u2019t prohibit these strategies or mention anything explicitly regarding them, but they are frowned upon and can lead to unwanted results. However, they won\u2019t get your website banned from search engines. So, we can say that the content you create and publish according to gray-hat SEO is ill-defined. Common examples of gray-hat SEO are excessive or suspicious links, clickbait content to sensationalize it, paid reviews, etc. Although these practices are not forbidden, avoiding such underhanded techniques is better.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/seo-course?utm_source=WsBlog&amp;utm_medium=Content_Banner&amp;utm_campaign=SEO&amp;utm_page=\/seo-types\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1000\" height=\"210\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course.webp\" alt=\"seo course\" class=\"wp-image-11966\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course.webp 1000w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course-300x63.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/07\/seo-course-768x161.webp 768w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\" \/><\/a><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Conclusion<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>It\u2019s crucial to understand the main types of SEO in digital marketing to improve your website\u2019s online visibility and search engine rankings. From on-page and off-page SEO to voice SEO to international SEO to technical SEO, each plays a vital role in SEO marketing campaigns. On-page SEO optimizes the website, while technical SEO ensures the smooth functionality of the site. Similarly, off-page SEO builds page authority, and international SEO takes your business to the global level. Make sure you navigate each of these SEO methods effectively and use the right technique to attract more traffic and foster sustainable business growth.&nbsp;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-vivid-cyan-blue-background-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color wp-elements-3cf06b6cdda66c085d83d8acd0831a8e\"><strong